; e106_reject_length.chiral — E106 conformance: REJECTION 2 of 4.
;
; The unrestricted `length`/`count` idiom — take the container, read a number,
; and DISCARD the container ("how many do I hold" as a free borrow) — is rejected
; over a linear container: the binder `v` is declared quantity `1` (linear, holds
; N caps) but the body drops it, leaking every cap. This is precisely why
; `sv-count` threads the vector back inside `CountR` instead of returning a bare
; `I64`. The dropped LAMBDA binder trips strip-binder (kernel.chiral:313).
; Expected B1 verdict: `load: linear binder usage mismatch`.
(import "prelude/prelude")
(import "ports/ports")
(import "capability/lincoll")

(def bad-count (-> (1 v SockVec) I64)
  (lam (v) 0))   ; v (the linear vector) dropped: a free count that leaks the caps
